---
description: UI and UX standards
globs: "app/**"
alwaysApply: true
---

## UI Rules
- Use NativeWind only
- No StyleSheet unless animation/perf critical
- No hardcoded text → use i18n
- Use lucide-react-native for icons

## UX Rules
- Designed for non-technical users
- Prefer clarity over density
- Dashboard = summary first, drill-down later

## Charts
- All charts must use ChartContainer
- Handle loading, empty, error states
##UX coding Rules
- Hooks must expose stable, descriptive state names.
- UI must not rename hook return values unless absolutely necessary.
- Screens MUST NOT import services or container.ts.
- Screens MUST use hooks for all business interactions.
- Hooks are the only UI-adjacent layer allowed to access services.
